{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1787148830,"nonce":"dSRdyzYdI65tZZRWvdBuG8IIAoE=","message":"**One of the four things this ticket asks someone to observe no longer exists, and the rest of the ticket got stronger because of it.**\n\nThe `@`-mention clause is now unverifiable rather than unverified. This ticket says, in **What is wrong**, *\"An `@`-mention that actually notifies. Amendment 3 ships `unacked_reminder_mention` on the strength of Slack's documentation alone\"*, and its **Done when** requires *\"an `@`-mention that fires a notification on a locked phone\"*. `4f5204f` deleted the entire mention surface: `RenderOptions.Mentions`, `WithMentions`, the renderer's `For` method, `mentionList`, `mentionTokenRe`, `channels.config.mention_on_reminder`, the `Mentions` port field, and all four `unacked_reminder*` org settings keys. `docs/adr/0020-*.md:4` now carries the supersession in its own header: *\"⛔ Amendment 3 SUPERSEDED 2026-08-20: the unacked reminder and its mention audience are REMOVED\"*. **There is no mention for anyone to observe.** That clause should be struck when this ticket is next edited; I have not edited the body, because the body is the historical record of what was believed at filing time and this comment is the correction.\n\n**The other three still stand exactly as written**, and nothing in `ec9dee4`, `4784fd0`, `263ee52` or `4f5204f` touched them: `chat.update` of a root, a threaded reply, the resolved/snoozed card variants, and client parity have still never been seen against a real workspace.\n\n⚠️ **And a fourth thing has quietly joined the list of what cannot be observed.** `git grep -nI 'ReasonRefired' -- '*.go'` outside tests returns eight lines and all eight are vocabulary, classification or rendering — `reason.go:52,59,119,258,315`, `verbosity.go:52`, `broadcast.go:101`, `service/view.go:382`. Nothing constructs a notification with it; ADR 0040 retired T8 and `broadcast.go:71` says so itself: *\"⛔ RETAINED FOR HISTORY; NOTHING PRODUCES IT.\"* With `all_resolved` opt-in and default-off, **`BroadcastPolicy.Warrants` is one unproducible Reason and one Reason nobody has switched on — so oto broadcasts nothing out of the box.** The title of this ticket is *\"Slack beyond the broadcast is still unobserved\"*, and the broadcast itself is now in the same position: `reply_broadcast: true` is a parameter ADR 0020 Amendment 4 had to CORRECT from a live workspace, and today there is no default path that would exercise it again.\n\n⭐ **Which is why this ticket is worth more than when it was filed, not less.** It is the standing record that the `@`-mention path was never once observed working, and that record was load-bearing three times over in `bd0fb1d`'s reasoning: removing a surface nobody had ever seen function is cheap, and it was only knowable as cheap because this ticket wrote the absence down. Keeping the ticket open with the mention clause corrected preserves that, where editing the clause away would erase it.\n\n**Still refused for the reason it was filed with:** it needs a human with real workspace credentials. Three unattended sessions in a row have declined it on that ground, this one included. `docs/setup/slack.md` remains the checklist.","files":null}]}